In article <4859@czech.sw.mcc.com> daneman@czech.sw.mcc.com (Michael Daneman) writes:
>
>What is Nethack and how is it different form regular hack (which I
>have finsihed once, I'm no dummy).

'Net' in NetHack simply referrs to the fact that it's being developed
over the net.  It's the successor to hack, based on hack's source
code.

Have you ever tried Rogue?
Hack:Rogue :: NetHack:Hack

Some basic starting information for you:
The current version is NetHack 3.0j pl10.
NetHack 3.1 is under development.
The ftp site for NetHack is linc.cis.upenn.edu
 The source is stored in /pub/NH3.0
 The PC compiled binaries are in /pub/NH3.0/PC
 The Macintosh binaries in /pub/NH3.0/Mac, etc.
The development team's address is nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu

